WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:09.740
A group of bandits loaded a cart with food the next day.

2
00:00:09.741 --> 00:00:13.111
Gildong led them into town.

3
00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:19.776
The buildings looked shabby.

4
00:00:19.777 --> 00:00:23.712
The market stalls were mostly empty.

5
00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:29.149
"This town is really poor," Gildong thought.

6
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.824
An old, thin woman was in the street.

7
00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:38.145
"Do you need some rice?" Nabi held out a small sack.

8
00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:42.913
The woman's eyes lit up. "Thank you!"

9
00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:49.005
A few people gathered around the cart.

10
00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:54.331
The thieves handed out more rice.

11
00:00:54.332 --> 00:00:58.275
"Boknam!" a little girl cried.

12
00:00:58.276 --> 00:01:02.470
She ran toward the cart.

13
00:01:02.471 --> 00:01:08.155
"Soonhee! We have food!" Boknam said.

14
00:01:08.156 --> 00:01:12.961
Gildong grabbed a few sacks of rice.

15
00:01:12.962 --> 00:01:17.225
"Here, you can take these home."

16
00:01:17.226 --> 00:01:21.192
"We don't have a house anymore," Soonhee said.

17
00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:23.588
"Oh," Gildong said.

18
00:01:23.589 --> 00:01:28.127
"Then you can stay with us from now on."

19
00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:33.182
While the other bandits handed out food, Gildong looked around.

20
00:01:33.183 --> 00:01:36.522
"I wonder if anyone sells books," he thought.

21
00:01:36.523 --> 00:01:43.776
But he didn't see any books in the market.

22
00:01:43.777 --> 00:01:47.164
He went to a candlemaker's stall to ask.

23
00:01:47.165 --> 00:01:51.873
Suddenly a farmer pushed Gildong aside.

24
00:01:51.874 --> 00:01:54.606
"You sold me bad candles!"

25
00:01:54.607 --> 00:01:57.822
The farmer yelled at the young candlemaker.

26
00:01:57.823 --> 00:02:01.008
He tossed some candles to the ground.

27
00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.282
They cracked open and dirt spilled out.

28
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.936
"Give me back my money!"

29
00:02:07.937 --> 00:02:11.268
The young man shook with fear.

30
00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:16.576
"I'm sorry. I don't have much wax, and I need money quickly."

31
00:02:16.577 --> 00:02:19.807
Gildong stepped in front of the farmer.

32
00:02:19.808 --> 00:02:22.047
He held out some coins.

33
00:02:22.048 --> 00:02:25.439
"Does this cover the cost of the candles you bought?"

34
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.732
The farmer took the coins and nodded.

35
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:37.713
"If this guy cheats anyone else, I'll report him to an official!"

36
00:02:37.714 --> 00:02:40.648
The candlemaker looked at Gildong.

37
00:02:40.649 --> 00:02:43.323
"Thank you for helping me."

38
00:02:43.324 --> 00:02:45.924
"It's okay," Gildong said.

39
00:02:45.925 --> 00:02:49.660
"But why do you need money so quickly?"

40
00:02:49.661 --> 00:02:53.692
"I needed food for my sick mother," the man said.

41
00:02:53.693 --> 00:02:57.250
"So I borrowed a small sack of rice from a landowner.

42
00:02:57.251 --> 00:03:00.178
Now I must pay him back."

43
00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:05.387
"I can help you repay him," Gildong said.

44
00:03:05.388 --> 00:03:10.143
They went to the cart, and Gildong grabbed a sack of rice.

45
00:03:10.144 --> 00:03:13.154
The candlemaker looked sheepish.

46
00:03:13.155 --> 00:03:16.435
"I also have to pay him interest.

47
00:03:16.436 --> 00:03:20.373
Every day the rice I owe doubles."

48
00:03:20.374 --> 00:03:22.809
Gildong blinked.

49
00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.692
"You only borrowed one small sack of rice.

50
00:03:25.693 --> 00:03:28.573
How many days has it been?"

51
00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:38.075
"Twenty-two," the man said nervously.

52
00:03:38.076 --> 00:03:43.177
"That's a lot of rice!" Gildong was shocked.

53
00:03:43.178 --> 00:03:44.824
"I need to pay soon.

54
00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:49.970
Or the landowner will make me his servant," the candlemaker said.

55
00:03:49.971 --> 00:03:52.729
Gildong shook his head.

56
00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:59.938
"The landowner is really unfair. Let's go talk to him."

